# Docs freshness

When editing code in the mapped areas below, also review and (if needed)
update the listed docs in the same change. Do not update docs
proactively when no corresponding code changes.

## Code area → docs map (Bot)

- `bot/handlers/web_auth.py`, `bot/api/internal.py`, anything importing
  `dotsound_private_core` policy functions →
  `docs/ai-boundary-policy.md`, `docs/private-boundary-inventory.md`,
  `docs/private-core-dependency-policy.md`.
- `bot/api/client.py`, `bot/handlers/*` that call Backend endpoints →
  `docs/private-core-dependency-policy.md` when new private imports are
  added or removed.
- `bot/main.py` dispatcher wiring, new handlers/middlewares →
  re-read the layout diagram in `README.md` (Bot) to keep it honest.

## Cross-repo variants

Files with the same name in Backend and PrivateCore
(`docs/ai-boundary-policy.md`, `docs/private-boundary-inventory.md`,
`docs/private-core-dependency-policy.md`, `docs/public-release-cut.md`)
are **per-repo variants**, not byte-copies. When editing this repo's
variant, check whether the change affects scope claims in Backend or
PrivateCore variants and update them if it does.

## Hard rule

Never put PrivateCore internals (provider names, model names, pipeline
stages, scoring weights) into any Bot doc. Use opaque language.
